Subject: The profiler names a read two prototypes up apart from a direct prototype read

What this does
  - `regvm_pic_fill` passes `REG_PIC_PROTO2` to the profile for a holder two prototypes up, and
    `REG_PIC_PROTO` only for a direct prototype (profile builds only).

Why we need it
  A direct prototype read is served by the function's own cache entry and a compiled body can read it
  inline; a read two prototypes up is only in the global stub cache, so it never hits there. The profile
  recorded both as the same kind, so the generator could not tell which sites a body may group.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -24619,7 +24619,10 @@
         return;
 
     rsh = p->shape;
-    AOT_PROF_PIC(b, site, rsh, depth == 0 ? REG_PIC_OWN : REG_PIC_PROTO);
+    /* A read two prototypes up is cached only by the global stub cache, never by the
+       function's own cache entry, so the profile names it apart from a direct prototype. */
+    AOT_PROF_PIC(b, site, rsh,
+                 depth == 0 ? REG_PIC_OWN : depth == 1 ? REG_PIC_PROTO : REG_PIC_PROTO2);
     slot = (uint32_t)(pr - holder->prop);
 
     /* A depth-0/1 site hashes its receiver shape (see regvm_shape_hashify);
